WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.925
Now with numbers.

2
00:00:02.175 --> 00:00:04.025
Follow the diagram.

3
00:00:04.275 --> 00:00:07.675
You want to make good a track of zero nine zero true.

4
00:00:07.925 --> 00:00:10.250
Your boat speed is ten knots.

5
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.400
The current sets one eight zero at two knots.

6
00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:15.550
It’s pushing you south.

7
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:17.350
Step one.

8
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:21.050
From the start, draw two miles toward one eight zero.

9
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.875
Step two.

10
00:00:23.125 --> 00:00:27.375
From the end of that line, swing ten miles until you hit the track.

11
00:00:27.625 --> 00:00:33.200
Before we measure it, which way do you expect to steer: north of east, or south of east?

12
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.550
North.

13
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.200
You have to point up into the current.

14
00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:40.725
And that’s what the drawing shows.

15
00:00:40.975 --> 00:00:43.950
The line runs about zero seven eight true.

16
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:48.775
You steer zero seven eight, crabbing about twelve degrees into the current.

17
00:00:49.025 --> 00:00:53.575
And your speed made good along the track is about nine point eight knots.

18
00:00:53.825 --> 00:00:58.575
A little less than ten, because some of your effort is spent holding the line.
